2025-05-05 03:58:51 - Thread-2523 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Here is a step-by-step set of SQLs – from very simple explorations to the final summary – showing how to obtain the number of distinct Austin B-Cycle (bike-share) stations that were Active or Closed during 2013 and 2014.

```sql
--Description: 1) Preview distinct values that appear in the `status` column
SELECT DISTINCT `status`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) See a few rows that were modified in 2013 to confirm the data we’re working with
SELECT `station_id`, `name`, `status`, `modified_date`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2013
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Inspect the same for 2014
SELECT `station_id`, `name`, `status`, `modified_date`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Count DISTINCT stations in 2013 that were ever marked Active
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`) AS active_stations_2013
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2013
  AND LOWER(`status`) = 'active';
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Count DISTINCT stations in 2013 that were ever marked Closed
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`) AS closed_stations_2013
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2013
  AND LOWER(`status`) = 'closed';
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Count DISTINCT stations in 2014 that were ever marked Active
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`) AS active_stations_2014
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2014
  AND LOWER(`status`) = 'active';
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count DISTINCT stations in 2014 that were ever marked Closed
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`) AS closed_stations_2014
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2014
  AND LOWER(`status`) = 'closed';
```

```sql
--Description: 8) FINAL ANSWER – side-by-side counts of distinct Active vs Closed stations for 2013 & 2014
SELECT
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`)        AS year,
  LOWER(`status`)                           AS station_status,
  COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`)              AS num_distinct_stations
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) IN (2013, 2014)
  AND LOWER(`status`) IN ('active', 'closed')
GROUP BY year, station_status
ORDER BY year, station_status
LIMIT 20;
```

Running the last query will return a small two-row result for each year that looks like this (example):

year | station_status | num_distinct_stations  
---- | -------------- | ----------------------  
2013 | active         | XX  
2013 | closed         | YY  
2014 | active         | AA  
2014 | closed         | BB  

Replace XX / YY / AA / BB with the actual counts returned by BigQuery.
